Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Surface provider call failures in the task log

Reason: Every HTTP failure inside `chat_complete` -- a 429 that costs a backoff
sleep, a 402 that rotates to the next key, a timeout that is retried, a tier
whose keys are all daily-locked -- was recorded only in the `api_attempts` array
of a task artifact. Nothing reached the reporter, so from the desktop a rate
limited or out-of-balance provider is indistinguishable from a hung stage, and
the support answer had to be "send me the artifacts directory". The first
occurrence of each (tier, model, return code) is a warning that keeps the
provider's own error text and says what happens next; repeats degrade to debug,
because a rate limited run is expected to produce a stream of them.

Removal: Delete once upstream routes provider failures through the reporter.

diff --git a/src/finesub/llm/llm_runtime.py b/src/finesub/llm/llm_runtime.py
